          "IOTA and OMEGA: (saluting) For the glory of Mars, Oop! : Yes, of course! (unhappily) Immediately. (He opens his OOP mouth wide. Omega and Iota watch him breathlessly. He bites down on a corner of the book, and pantomimes chewing and swallowing, while making terrible faces.)",
          "OMEGA: Well, Oop? : Well, Oop? (Oop coughs. Omega and Iota pound him on IOTA the back.)",
          "THINK-TANK: Was it not delicious, Sergeant Oop? : (saluting) That is correct, sir. It was not delicious. I OOP don’t know how the Earthlings can get those sandwiches down without water. They’re dry as Martian dust.",
          "NOODLE: Sir, sir. Great and Mighty Think-Tank. I beg your pardon, but an insignificant bit of data floated into my mind about those sandwiches.",
          "THINK-TANK: It can’t be worth much, but go ahead. Give us your trifling bit of data.",
          "NOODLE: Well, sir, I have seen surveyor films of those sandwiches. I noticed that the Earthlings did not eat them. They used them as some sort of communication device. : (haughtily) Naturally. That was my next point. These THINK-TANK are actually communication sandwiches. Think-Tank is never wrong. Who is never wrong? : (saluting) Great and Mighty Think-Tank is never wrong. ALL",
          "THINK-TANK: Therefore, I order you to listen to them.",
          "OMEGA: Listen to them? : (to each other, puzzled) Listen to them? IOTA AND OOP",
          "THINK-TANK: Do you have marbles in your ears? I said, listen to them. (Martians bow very low.) : It shall be done, sir. (They each take two books from OMEGA the case, and hold them to their ears, listening intently.) : (whispering to Omega) Do you hear anything? IOTA : (whispering back) Nothing. Do you hear anything, Oop? OMEGA : (loudly) Not a thing! (Omega and Iota jump in fright.) OOP : Sh-h-h! (They listen intently again.) OMEGA AND IOTA",
